          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mtikw6jh192zlcvn",
          "message": {
            "text": "The aggregate no-motion cap was remeasured rather than broadly relaxed. Chromium 147 produces 94 px largest and 1636 px total on the correct two-pane render, unchanged with GPU disabled; the deliberate paint-order break remains 3712 px and still exceeds the unchanged 256 px component cap. Therefore 2048 admits current scattered edge noise without admitting the known structural failure.",
            "markdown": "The aggregate no-motion cap was remeasured rather than broadly relaxed. Chromium 147 produces 94 px largest and 1636 px total on the correct two-pane render, unchanged with GPU disabled; the deliberate paint-order break remains 3712 px and still exceeds the unchanged 256 px component cap. Therefore 2048 admits current scattered edge noise without admitting the known structural failure."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/review/compare-pngs.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 781,
                  "endLine": 800,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " *  Chromium 147 changed path-edge rasterization between a direct frame and the\n *  equivalent animated layer. Re-measuring the current 900x420 two-pane corpus\n *  on macOS gives a clean ceiling of 94 px for one component and 1636 px in\n *  total, still with `regionCount === 0`; disabling GPU compositing produces\n *  the same result. The known out-of-position-reopen break remains separated:\n *  3712 px with `regionCount === 0`, including a component larger than the\n *  unchanged 256 px single-region cap. The 2048 aggregate cap therefore admits\n *  the measured scattered text-edge floor without admitting that structural\n *  paint-order failure.\n *\n *  Unlike the visual gate's per-platform hinting floor (\"Per-platform coverage\n *  floor\" in docs/12-diff-scoring.md), this bar needs no per-platform relief:\n *  there both images come from DIFFERENT rasterizers, so the host's text\n *  rendering is inherently part of the measurement; here both come from ours. */\nexport interface StrictCaps {\n  maxRegionArea: number;\n  totalRegionArea: number;\n}\nexport function strictCapsFor(_platform: NodeJS.Platform | string): StrictCaps {\n  return { maxRegionArea: 256, totalRegionArea: 2048 };"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
